// A2 gate (Hβ.emit.variant-payload-repr-width) — a variant with an f64 payload
// round-trips at FULL PRECISION through CONSTRUCT + MATCH-BIND + EQ + SHOW, the
// four reading ONE width-summed payload-offset fold (variant_payload_offset,
// starting after the 4-byte tag). A variant payload was UNIFORM-i32-slotted
// (store/eq/match at 4+4*i i32) — so an f64 payload was truncated to its low 4
// bytes. The migration makes all four agree at the payload's PROVEN repr:
//   - store:     emit_variant_stores_acc (f64.store at the width-summed offset)
//   - eq-leaf:   emit_eq_variant_payload_conjunction (f64.load + f64.eq)
//   - match-bind: emit_pat_con_subs_binds reads ctor_payload_tys_of(name),
//                 binds at repr_of(payload_ty) (f64.load via emit_load_chain_repr)
//   - show:      emit_show_variant_payload_render (f64.load + float_to_str)
// One offset+width fact, four projections — an f64 payload is genuinely 8 bytes.
//
// `Measure(2.5)` constructed; `Measure(v) => v` binds 2.5 via the width-aware
// match-bind reading the same f64 the store wrote.
//
// THE SEED LAGS THIS FORM (the hand-WAT emit slots variant payloads uniform-i32
// and floors f64 — the same lag mn-repr-record / mn-float-arith document). So the
// VALUE gate runs through MENTL2 (the wheel compiled by the seed, carrying the
// wheel's width-summed payload store/load), NOT the seed directly. Named peer:
// Hβ.seed.variant-payload-repr — the seed mirrors the width-summed payload
// store/eq/match/show when next required, the .mn leading until then (PLAN §5).
//
// Expected exit 5: Measure(2.5) destructured to 2.5, doubled = 5.0, truncated 5.

type Reading
  = Measure(Float)
  | Empty

fn value_of(r) = match r {
  Measure(v) => v + v,
  Empty      => 0.0
}

fn main(q) = {
  let r = Measure(2.5)
  value_of(r)
}
